       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen at 9,600 mg/day is three times the 3,200 mg/day maximum. I know of no indication that justifies it, and it could seriously harm the patient. Higher doses add no analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit, but they sharply raise the risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even when kidney and liver function are normal.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you have a specific reason for the higher dose, such as a protocol or a toxicology or pharmacy recommendation, please take it up with pharmacy directly. I'd also be glad to help you with a multimodal analgesic plan if pain control is the goal."
